    <cco:ont00001920 rdf:resource="http://example.org/llnl#preferred_citation"/>
    <skos:definition>[reusability_if_applicable] e.g., Available at \url{ark:/12345/abcde} For legacy bibtex entries (that don't accept eprinttype and eprint) and that need to support an ark or other identifiers that don't fit cleanly into the existing fields, the note field can be used to capture this information in a free-text format. include a note: field use this format for the note field: note: Available at \url{ark:/12345/abcde} --- Integrity &amp; Fixity ----------------------------------------- [reusability_if_applicable] Checksums enable automated validation of data integrity after transfer or storage.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>note</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000853"/>
  </rdf:Description>
